...
if (dev_path_len > out_len) {
    ret = -ENOSPC;
    goto end;
}
kfree(dev_path); // only after successful copy
Reason:
The function allocates memory for dev_path via kobject_get_path. If the path length exceeds the output buffer, it jumps to end without freeing the allocated memory, causing a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
